WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.368
Skills: procedures that load on demand.

2
00:00:02.648 --> 00:00:04.504
A skill is a folder with a SKILL.

3
00:00:04.784 --> 00:00:11.440
md file: YAML frontmatter, then instructions, optionally with supporting files and scripts beside it.

4
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.128
Project skills live in.

5
00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:17.568
claude/skills/<name>/, personal ones in ~/.

6
00:00:17.848 --> 00:00:19.405
claude/skills/.

7
00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:26.341
You invoke one by typing /name, or Claude loads it automatically when your request matches its description.

8
00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:30.397
Custom slash commands have been folded into skills: a file in.

9
00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:32.789
claude/commands/deploy.

10
00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:34.520
md still works, but.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.360
claude/skills/deploy/SKILL.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:43.891
md adds supporting files, invocation control, and automatic loading, and wins if both exist.

13
00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:50.080
The description is the most important line you write, because it’s all Claude sees until the skill is used.

14
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.435
Say what the skill does and when to use it, in the words a user would type.

15
00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:59.045
Vague or overlapping descriptions mean the wrong skill loads, or none does.

16
00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.461
Two frontmatter fields matter most for safety and cost.

17
00:01:02.741 --> 00:01:14.027
disable-model-invocation: true means only you can start the skill, and its description stays out of context until you do: use it for anything with side effects, like cutting a release.

18
00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:17.891
allowed-tools pre-approves specific tools while the skill runs.

19
00:01:18.171 --> 00:01:27.045
Others let a skill run in a forked subagent ( context: fork ), pick a model or effort, or limit automatic activation to certain paths.

20
00:01:27.325 --> 00:01:35.368
Claude Code also ships bundled skills such as /code-review, /simplify, /debug, /batch, and /verify.

21
00:01:35.648 --> 00:01:36.544
Keep SKILL.

22
00:01:36.824 --> 00:01:46.360
md under about 500 lines and move detail into sibling files it points to; the same “only write what it can’t figure out” rule from CLAUDE.

23
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:47.707
md applies.
